# Ancient Adamantoise: "All damage that would be dealt to you and other permanents you control is dealt to this creature
# instead" (CR 614.1a), and "Damage isn't removed from this creature during cleanup steps" (CR 514.2). Bot2 attacks with
# Bofur (1/1 lifelink) unblocked and Woodland Changeling (2/2), which Bot1's Llanowar Elves blocks. Bofur's combat damage to
# Bot1 and the Changeling's to the Elves are both dealt to the Adamantoise instead, still combat damage from the same
# sources (the rulings): Bot1 loses no life and the Elves live, and Bofur's lifelink still gains Bot2 1 life (CR
# 702.15b). The Elves' 1 damage to the Changeling is no redirect's business. In Bot2's cleanup the Changeling's damage
# wears off and the Adamantoise's does not; it is still there in Bot1's next turn, and after Bot1's own cleanup too. The
# Adamantoise attacks in between and stays untapped (vigilance).

[Bot1 Deck]
